            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0454" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 European War 1939/1371: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-02T13:00:00+03:25">September 2, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 3—10:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. The Turkish Chargé d’Affaires informs me he received this morning new
                    instructions from his Government authorizing him to grant refuge to Germans only
                    in occupied parts of Iran. This would preclude the granting of asylum to Germans
                    here and avoid the complication mentioned in my number 130.<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d433-f1"/></p>
                <p>This relieves a situation which was being viewed most seriously by the Iranian
                    Government and the British Legation replies to Ankara.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
